## Unresolved / notes

- One real defect was found and fixed in the library during verification: `check`'s wait branch originally destructured the poll result without testing it, conj'ing a `nil` wake and never retaining the entry. Now `if-some` splits wake from wait. All other fixes were test-side (a delimiter imbalance; a wrong probe expectation — the sweep does call the probe's identity `:advance` once, which the test now asserts alongside the byte-identical store).
